From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: the rectangle suggested for a new display scale fits the work area

WM_DPICHANGED's suggested rectangle (0890) was the window at the new
scale, kept on the screen by moving it -- but not made smaller: Settings,
1000x700 at 100% on a 1280x800 screen, was suggested 1500x1050 at 150%
and ran off the screen. It is now no larger than the monitor's work area.

Test: test/dpilive-gate.sh (a 1800x1100 per-monitor v2 window at 175% on
2736x1824; mutant SG_MUTANT_DPI_RECT_UNCLAMPED).
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -6591,6 +6591,12 @@
     if (!IsRectEmpty( &info.rcWork ))
     {
         RECT work = info.rcWork;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DPI_RECT_UNCLAMPED
+        /* no larger than the work area: a window that fit at 100% fits at
+         * 150% too (Settings on a 1280x800 screen ran off it) */
+        if (rect.right - rect.left > work.right - work.left) rect.right = rect.left + work.right - work.left;
+        if (rect.bottom - rect.top > work.bottom - work.top) rect.bottom = rect.top + work.bottom - work.top;
+#endif
         if (rect.right > work.right) OffsetRect( &rect, max( work.right - rect.right, work.left - rect.left ), 0 );
         if (rect.bottom > work.bottom) OffsetRect( &rect, 0, max( work.bottom - rect.bottom, work.top - rect.top ) );
     }
